{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review repair for your #13 work (same worktree and branch). Do not delegate further. One commit, do not push.\n\n1. bin/setup.sh: after moving the old profile, `rmdir` the old `cursor-delegate` config dir if it is now empty (ignore failure).\n2. Over-engineering hypotheses. Apply each ONLY if it removes code and `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test` stay green with tests/cli_e2e.rs, tests/cli_info_e2e.rs, tests/budgets.rs unchanged. Skip any that adds lines or changes CLI behaviour, and say why:\n   a. src/prompt.rs: delete `verify_block`/`compose_prompt` and their tests if only `status_block` is used.\n   b. src/job.rs: drop the empty `WaitOpts` parameter from `dispatch`/`wait`.\n   c. src/job.rs + src/types.rs: drop the synchronous dispatch path (`background`, `wait_ms`, `DispatchResult::Output`, `Detached.busy_path`) so dispatch always detaches and returns the job id.\n   d. src/types.rs: delete `RunOutput.downgraded`.\n   e. src/status_record.rs: delete `NoopStatusWriter` if unused outside tests (tests may use a local stub).\n   f. src/job.rs: replace the injectable `FinalizeFn` pair on `JobDeps` with direct `finalize_run`/`finalize_stall` calls, unless a kept test needs the seam.\nCommit `refactor: drop MCP-era seams left in the supervisor (#13 review)` ending `Co-Authored-By: Composer 2.5 <noreply@cursor.com>`.\n\nCompletion bar: commit SHA, `git diff --stat HEAD~1` summary line, a/b/c/d/e/f applied-or-skipped with one-line reason each, test counts. Then **Friction** (≤3 bullets). End with a STATUS line.\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"e2d994f1-ef61-48a1-b218-cde928b7cc82"}
